== Effect ==
* Spawns one [[coin]] of any type upon taking damage.
** {{dlc|r}} When held by {{C|Keeper}} and {{C|Tainted Keeper}}, spawns 0-1 coins.

== Notes ==
* This trinket can be found by destroying [[Rocks#Urns|urns]], {{E|Special Shopkeeper}}s, and {{dlc+|r}} [[Rocks#Buckets|buckets]] in {{s|Downpour}}.{{dlc-}}
* Though similar to the {{i|Piggy Bank}} item, the Swallowed Penny is not limited to just pennies.
* {{dlc|anr}} Unlike {{i|Piggy Bank}}, playing as {{C|Keeper}} with this trinket always drops a coin, allowing semi-infinite life.
** A trick for farming money when playing as Keeper is to find a room with some static hazard like spikes and taking damage, causing a coin to appear. A penny will only refill life while a nickel will give four cents, and a dime will give nine cents.
*** This trick can also be used to survive multiple uses of a sacrifice room, healing with the dropped coin between each sacrifice.
** {{Dlc|r}} As it can now give 0 coins when playing as the Keeper, this no longer works. The {{i|Piggy Bank}} and {{i|IV Bag}} also spawn 0-1 coins when damage is taken; with all three, though money is no longer guaranteed, if a large pool of coins is found it can be used to mitigate streaks of bad luck, allowing Keeper to farm coins almost reliably.

== Synergies ==
* {{I|Mom's Box|nr}}: Spawns two coins on hit, multiple copies don't stack.
* {{A|Golden Trinket}} / {{I|Mom's Box|r}}: Each copy spawns one more coin on getting hit with a limit of 5 coins.
** {{dlc|r}} This does not add another 0-1 chance as {{C|Keeper|n}} or {{C|Tainted Keeper|n}}.

